            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com Can you please address comments and resolve merge conflicts on this patch. Thanks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "done."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/interface.cpp",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I think your filenames are not reflecting the intent of the code. This file or class is the one which creates different types of Lattice CPLD interfaces, as you have started doing now at line#18, so i would consider this class to be LatticeFactory rather than interface. \nHaving said that the CpldLatticeManager is more of a LatticeInterface instead since different Lattice CPLD updaters are going to inherit and implement that interface, isn't it?\nIf you agree with what i mentioned my suggestion is to rename these files accordingly so we can avoid this confusion. Since, now you are adding more types of Lattice CPLDs now is the right time to do it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/interface.cpp",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "would do."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/interface.cpp",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Renamed LatticeCPLDInterface to LatticeCPLDFactory, since this class mainly instantiates the corresponding CPLDDevice class via its constructor to handle the update() and getVersion() functions. Also renamed the original CPLDManager and XO2XO3UpdateFlow to LatticeBaseCPLD and LatticeXO3CPLD, respectively."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "lets change this from chipName to chipModel instead."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "would do."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Since enums do not support strings, an enum_to_string function is needed. Therefore, I removed the chipModel string and let the enum_to_string function handle cases where the chip model string is required."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Lets define an enum for this and call the enum chipFamily. Choose the right updater based on chip family. Fix at other places in the code also based on this idea."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "They can all be changed to enums, but since enums don\u2019t support strings, an additional toString function will inevitably be needed for maintenance."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "done."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "lets define an enum for chipType as well and use that everywhere rather than passing strings around. This is kind of becoming unmanageable given the number of types being added."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "They can all be changed to enums, but since enums don\u2019t support strings, an additional toString function will inevitably be needed for maintenance."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 89,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is readUserCode protected? i see getVersion use to call it earlier."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 89,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "You are correct \u2014 the derived class does not need to call base::readUserCode(). Therefore, its access level can be changed to private or delete it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/lattice.hpp",
                    "line": 89,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/xo2xo3.hpp",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "What is the difference between X02X03 and X05 update flows. I am thinking we need to name this better so in future we don't have to change the file names again if another X0x chip model needs to use the same method again. Do you see such a use case in future?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/xo2xo3.hpp",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "I checked the SPEC, and Lattice did not specifically name these update flows; they are simply organized by device. I can only name the files as updateFlowA.hpp, updateFlowB.hpp, \u2026, or use a single updateFlows.hpp file, but it would still contain class updateFlowA, class updateFlowB."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/lattice/xo2xo3.hpp",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Changed to LatticeXO3CPLD. Since there is no specific name and the main chips used are from the XO3 family, while XO2 also shares this update flow but is not reflected in the LatticeXO3CPLD naming, the logic is handled in code (in lattice/interface.hpp)\n\n    switch (chipFamily)\n    {\n        case latticeChipFamily::XO2:\n        case latticeChipFamily::XO3:\n            return std::make_unique<LatticeXO3CPLD>(\n                CPLDInterface::ctx, CPLDInterface::bus, CPLDInterface::address,\n                chipModelStr, \"CFG0\", false);"
                }
            ],
